  "question": {
    "text": "The increase in pressure required to decrease the volume of a water sample by $0.2 \\%$ is $\\mathrm{P} \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{Nm}^{-2}$. Bulk modulus of water is $2.15 \\times 10^9 \\mathrm{Nm}^{-2}$. The value of P is $\\ldots\\ldots$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "43",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since bulk modulus is given as\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{B}=\\frac{-\\Delta \\mathrm{P}}{\\left(\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{~V}}{\\mathrm{~V}}\\right)} \\\\\n& 2.15 \\times 10^9=\\frac{-\\Delta \\mathrm{P}}{-\\left(\\frac{0.2}{100}\\right)} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{P}=2.15 \\times 10^9 \\times 2 \\times 10^{-3} \\\\\n& =4.3 \\times 10^6=43 \\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
